cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use seti-ellipsoid-broker in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "seti-ellipsoid-broker: an account-free SN 1987A SETI Ellipsoid target broker"
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline that computes which stars are currently crossing the SN 1987A
  SETI Ellipsoid — the locus from which a beacon synchronized to SN 1987A would reach
  Earth now — by fusing transient alerts with anonymous Gaia DR3 astrometry (including
  the Lindegren et al. 2021 parallax zero-point correction). Runs account-free via an
  externally-supplied transient list and exports ranked nightly observing targets.
  Crossing epochs are validated against the 217 SN 1987A targets of Nilipour et al. (2023).
